      "title": "Calculating a Unit Vector Parallel to a Given Vector"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "7b006ef4-67f4-5d41-9590-ddc805d688c9",
      ":question/problem": "Let $\\mathbf{r}=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf{r}$ and points the same direction.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{u} &= \\frac{\\mathbf{r}}{|\\mathbf{r}|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\mathbf{r}| &= \\sqrt{(8)^2+(-6)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{100} \\\\\n&= 10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $\\mathbf{r}$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{u} &= \\frac{\\mathbf{r}}{|\\mathbf{r}|} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{10}\\cdot (\\mathbf{r}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{10}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ - \\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
